\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Serving on real infrastructure.} (a)\nobreakspace  {}Feeding shape: per-chunk audio placeholders are out-of-distribution for a model trained on single segments (88\% WER); bounded re-feed of the last window costs a re-encode but is correct (3.8\%). (b)\nobreakspace  {}Per-chunk compute: the vLLM path is $5.4\times $ faster than the transformers simulator used for all pre-serving latency numbers; the max-segment force-flush also bounds the P95 tail. (c)\nobreakspace  {}Concurrent sessions per engine on a 0.15-GPU slice: flat to $N{=}8$, cliff at 16 --- the deadline binds, not memory.\relax }}{11}{figure.caption.28}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:serving}{{9}{11}{\textbf {Serving on real infrastructure.} (a)~Feeding shape: per-chunk audio placeholders are out-of-distribution for a model trained on single segments (88\% WER); bounded re-feed of the last window costs a re-encode but is correct (3.8\%). (b)~Per-chunk compute: the vLLM path is $5.4\times $ faster than the transformers simulator used for all pre-serving latency numbers; the max-segment force-flush also bounds the P95 tail. (c)~Concurrent sessions per engine on a 0.15-GPU slice: flat to $N{=}8$, cliff at 16 --- the deadline binds, not memory.\relax }{figure.caption.28}{}}
